- No main function needed, just script execution.
- Variables global or local.
- Input: `fscanf(STDIN, "%d %d\n", $n, $m);` or `explode` on `fgets`.
- Output: `echo $result . "\n";` or `print`.
- Logic loop: `for ($d = 1, $remain = $n; $remain > 0; $d++) { if ($d % $m != 0) $remain--; } $result = $d - 1;`

Need to handle input reading carefully in PHP.
`fscanf(STDIN, "%d %d", $n, $m);` works well.

Code structure:
<?php
$n = 0;
$m = 0;
$result = 0;

// in()
fscanf(STDIN, "%d %d", $n, $m);

// run()
$remain = $n;
$d = 1;
while ($remain > 0) {
    if ($d % $m != 0) {
        $remain--;
    }
    $d++;
}
$result = $d - 1;

// out()
echo $result . "\n";
?>

